# GFP_DMS/.gitignore
#
# Track the code needed to reproduce the best brightness model (cnn-max-d2, 40k classifier);
# skip the large / regenerable / externally-sourced artifacts.
#   KEEP  : transform/embed/subsample/classify scripts, notebooks, brightness_threshold.py,
#           README, figures.
#   IGNORE: the DMS datasets (raw + processed + subsample caches), ESM-2 embedding caches,
#           trained models, prediction caches, run logs, and the archived regression experiment.

# ---- DMS datasets & embedding caches (large; rebuild via transform_*/embed_parallel/build_subsample)
# Raw tables (.tsv, ortho .csv), processed *_sequences.csv, sub20k/sub40k caches, split CSV,
# ESM-2 per-residue arrays (~tens of GB) and the max-pool .npz caches. Covers all of DMS_data/.
DMS_data/*.csv
DMS_data/*.tsv
DMS_data/*.npy
DMS_data/*.npz
DMS_data/.embed_progress
DMS_data/.embed_progress.*

# ...except the small analysis caches lane A needs. These are the outputs of passes over the
# multi-GB embedding caches, not the caches themselves: keeping the ~1 MB of results in git is
# what lets the write-up notebook run without the 85 GB of ESM-2 embeddings behind them.
!DMS_data/heldout_scored.npz

# ---- Trained models & cached predictions (rebuild with sweep_classify_parallel.py) ----------
# Directory contents are ignored, with two exceptions re-included below. Note the `dir/*` form
# rather than `dir/`: git does not descend into an ignored directory, so a bare `trained_models/`
# would make the negations underneath it unreachable.
trained_models/*
!trained_models/sweep_class4/
trained_models/sweep_class4/*
# The sweep leaderboard and the top-5 validation logits: 66 KB together, and the only two things
# the write-up notebook needs from a 24-configuration sweep whose checkpoints total ~100 MB.
!trained_models/sweep_class4/results.csv
!trained_models/sweep_class4/val_logits_top5.npz

# ---- Archived regression experiment (superseded by the classifier pipeline) -----------------
archive_regression/

# ---- Superseded regression sweep (replaced by sweep_classify_parallel.py) --------------------
sweep_brightness.py

# ---- Run logs / scratch ----------------------------------------------------------------------
logs/
*.log

# ---- Python / Jupyter cruft ------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/
